-option(CRISPY_TRUECOLOR "True color rendering" OFF)
+# DOOMed Prism: the frame-export path (src/i_framebuffer_export.c) reads
+# argbbuffer->pixels to publish frames into shared memory. That is only a
+# safe, CPU-readable buffer in the CRISPY_TRUECOLOR path (a real
+# SDL_CreateRGBSurfaceWithFormat allocation the renderer draws into
+# directly). The default (truecolor off) path aliases argbbuffer->pixels to
+# a locked GPU streaming-texture region between SDL_LockTexture and
+# SDL_UnlockTexture, which is write-oriented on hardware-accelerated
+# renderers (observed to SIGSEGV on read against a Direct3D backend on
+# Windows) -- so this default is flipped to ON rather than left for callers
+# to remember to pass.
+option(CRISPY_TRUECOLOR "True color rendering" ON)
 
